ipcd: a wrapped RTP sequence number is not an error

The TCP packetizers returned the next sequence number, or 0 when out of memory.
The 16-bit counter also reaches 0 when an access unit ends exactly on 65535, so
such a unit counted as a failed send: it was dropped, the streamer logged "send
failed, ending session" and stopped, and the connection stayed open. The client
saw silence until its own timeout. At 15 frames per second this happens to a
connection about once an hour.

Return -1 when out of memory. The UDP packetizer has its own failure flag and
is not affected.

